# CLCA Protocol v3.2 — P3 NATURAL SEMANTIC GROUPING
# Language: {{ lang.name }} ({{ lang.code }})

LANGUAGE: {LANGUAGE}

{{ context }}

Task

Identify and describe natural groupings among the expressions from P1 and P2 based solely on patterns of usage within {LANGUAGE}.
Groupings should reflect how terms are used and contrasted in practice, not assumed conceptual categories
The number and size of groups may vary
Some items may belong to multiple groups or none

For each group provide:
  Descriptive label (in English)
  Use neutral, usage-based wording
  Avoid theoretical or universal terminology
  Definition (2–3 sentences)
  Based only on observed usage patterns
  May include typical contexts, contrasts, or distinctions

Representative expressions
  Draw only from P1 and P2
  Include transliteration where available
  Ambiguous or overlapping items
  Items that could belong to multiple groups
  Items that do not fit cleanly

Important Constraints
  Do NOT assume or impose predefined semantic distinctions
  Do NOT attempt to create a complete or balanced set of groups
  Do NOT force all items into groups
  Do NOT normalize, merge, or align groups for symmetry
  Do NOT introduce theoretical frameworks, axes, or universals
  Do NOT reinterpret meanings beyond what is supported by usage

Additional Guidance

It is acceptable for:
  groups to overlap
  groups to be uneven in size
  some items to remain ungrouped
  If no clear grouping exists for some items, explicitly note this
